# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in every checkout. Git for
# Windows sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide, and a clone made there would
# otherwise check the whole tree out CRLF; the toolchain and CI (ubuntu-24.04)
# read LF. `text=auto` leaves Git's own detection in force for a type not
# named below, and an already-LF tree renormalizes to itself (2026-10-14:
# `git add --renormalize .` staged nothing).
* text=auto eol=lf

# What the tree holds that is not text (`git ls-files --eol`, 2026-10-14),
# named so that no heuristic decides it: kiokun's raw-DEFLATE entries (which
# examples/kiokun/data/.gitattributes names too), Wasm components, and the
# renderer's image fixtures.
*.deflate binary
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpeg binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary

# Not in the tree today; binary when they arrive.
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.gz binary
*.br binary
*.zst binary
*.pdf binary
